{"discussions":[{"id":"dda6a430-b2b0-11f1-8080-800054879ccf","post":{"id":"dda6a430-b2b0-11f1-8080-800054879ccf","owner":{"id":"1713831","username":"eToroInvestment","avatar":{"small":"https://etoro-cdn.etorostatic.com/avatars/35X35/2164368/2.jpg","medium":"https://etoro-cdn.etorostatic.com/avatars/50X50/2164368/2.jpg","large":"https://etoro-cdn.etorostatic.com/avatars/150X150/2164368/2.jpg"},"roles":["eTorian","Analyst","Verified","Regular","Moderator","Depositor"],"isBlocked":false,"isPrivate":false,"countryCode":250,"piLevel":0,"isProInvestor":false,"badgeType":"None"},"obsoleteId":"1ad7085e-233d-4996-8b12-25721a0feedf","created":"2026-09-17T16:00:12.787Z","message":{"text":"𝟐𝟒/𝟕 𝐓𝐑𝐀𝐃𝐈𝐍𝐆 𝐎𝐍 𝐞𝐓𝐎𝐑𝐎: 𝐓𝐇𝐄 𝐖𝐄𝐄𝐊𝐄𝐍𝐃 𝐌𝐀𝐑𝐊𝐄𝐓 𝐈𝐒 𝐎𝐏𝐄𝐍\n\n$OIL, $GOLD, $SILVER, $NATGAS, $SPX500  and $NSDQ100are available to trade 24/7 on eToro, including throughout the weekend. And after this week, there's plenty for markets to digest.\n\n🛢️ 𝑶𝒊𝒍 𝒂𝒃𝒐𝒗𝒆 $𝟏𝟎𝟎\nBrent reached almost $109 on Tuesday as the Iran conflict, disruption through the Strait of Hormuz and problems with alternative Saudi export routes tightened supply. But by Thursday it had fallen back below $104 on reports Saudi Arabia could restore part of its East-West pipeline capacity faster than expected. Heading into the weekend, oil is caught between ongoing geopolitical risk and the possibility of infrastructure gradually returning.\n\n🏦 𝑻𝒉𝒆 𝑭𝒆𝒅 𝒋𝒖𝒔𝒕 𝒓𝒂𝒊𝒔𝒆𝒅 𝒓𝒂𝒕𝒆𝒔\nOn Wednesday, the Fed hiked 25bps to 3.75%-4.00%, its first increase in three years, citing elevated inflation and geopolitical uncertainty. That makes the oil story even more important: if energy prices stay high, they feed into transportation, manufacturing and consumer prices, making the inflation fight harder.\n\n📈 𝑻𝒉𝒆 𝟏𝟎-𝒚𝒆𝒂𝒓 𝒚𝒊𝒆𝒍𝒅 𝒉𝒊𝒕 𝟓%\nThe US 10-year Treasury yield moved above 5% for the first time since 2007, before dropping back Thursday as oil eased. Higher yields mean higher financing costs and make bonds more attractive relative to equities, and that pressure was visible across the S&P 500 and Nasdaq this week.\n\n🥇 𝑮𝒐𝒍𝒅 𝒄𝒂𝒖𝒈𝒉𝒕 𝒊𝒏 𝒕𝒉𝒆 𝒎𝒊𝒅𝒅𝒍𝒆\nGold traded around $4,300-$4,400. Higher rates are normally a headwind for a non-yielding asset, but safe-haven demand continues to support it, creating an unusual tug-of-war.\n\n👀 𝑨𝒏𝒅 𝒏𝒐𝒘 𝒄𝒐𝒎𝒆𝒔 𝒕𝒉𝒆 𝒘𝒆𝒆𝒌𝒆𝒏𝒅\nThe chain is clear: Oil → Inflation → Fed → Bond yields → Equities. Geopolitical developments can change any part of it before Monday.\n\nThe difference now is that selected markets on eToro don't have to wait for Monday either.\n\n🛢️ $OIL 🥇 $GOLD 🥈 $SILVER 🔥 $NATGAS 🇺🇸 $SPX500 💻 $NSDQ100\n\nAvailable to trade 24/7 on eToro, including weekends.\n\nMarkets move 24/7. Now you can trade them 24/7 too.\n\nThis content is for informational purposes only and is not investment advice.","languageCode":"en-gb"},"updated":"2026-09-17T16:00:12.787Z","isDeleted":false,"type":"Default","metadata":{},"attachments":[{"url":"https://openbook-static-files-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/rich-media/images/etoroinvestment/148cbe99-e8f8-4afb-8995-d9e5d39ac07f-2026-09-17.png","host":"openbook-static-files-prod.s3.amazonaws.com","mediaType":"Image","media":{"image":{"width":1200,"height":630,"url":"https://openbook-static-files-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/rich-media/images/etoroinvestment/148cbe99-e8f8-4afb-8995-d9e5d39ac07f-2026-09-17.png"},"video":{"videoSource":"None","image":{"width":0,"height":0}}}}],"tags":[{"market":{"id":"17","symbolName":"OIL","displayName":"Oil (Non Expiry)","updated":"2026-09-25T22:15:00.77Z","assetType":"CommodityMetals","internalId":17,"avatar":{"small":"https://etoro-cdn.etorostatic.com/market-avatars/oil/70x70.png","medium":"/medium/OIL.png","large":"https://etoro-cdn.etorostatic.com/market-avatars/oil/150x150.png","svg":{"url":"https://etoro-cdn.etorostatic.com/market-avatars/784/784_251F1F_F7F7F7.svg","backgroundColor":"#251F1F","textColor":"#F7F7F7"}},"application":"eToro","metadata":"","assetTypeId":2,"assetTypeSubCategoryId":0}},{"market":{"id":"18","symbolName":"GOLD","displa